food inventory test. And run the CLI command manually for the gate.\\n\\njustfile tier0: add line `cargo run --quiet -- doc-audit >/dev/null`? That runs the real audit each tier0 — cost fine (subprocess probes of missing binaries → binary_absent quickly; existing binaries like `wai`? not on PATH probably → absent). But scanning sibling repos — fine, read-only. Exit 0 unless loud error. Add after cargo test:\\n```\\ncargo run --quiet -- doc-audit\\n```\\nHmm prints JSON noise; redirect? Keep visible? just tier0 output verbosity ok, redirect to /dev/null but then rows invisible. Use `cargo run --quiet -- doc-audit > /dev/null`. I'll print a compact summary instead? Keep JSON full but redirect to /dev/null in justfile.\\n\\nWait — but maybe gate SHOULD fail on rows to \\\"flag drift\\\". Decide: measurement rows don't fail (report precedent), loud errors fail. Document in doc_audit header rationale. And \\\"flags the moment docs drift\\\" — rows appear in output every tier0 run. Acceptable.\\n\\nNow write tests/doc_audit.rs. Use tempfile? Check dev-dependencies.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9fdfa74d0e7a4b129b2a7748","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"dev-dependencies\" -A6 Cargo.toml; grep -rn \"tempfile\\|temp_dir\\|TempDir\" tests/*.rs src/*.rs | head; echo ---; sed -n 1,40p tests/report_aggregation.rs","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1285,"output":5016,"cacheRead":23552,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":4946,"totalTokens":29853,"cost":{"input":0.00019275,"output":0.002508,"cacheRead":0.00070656,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00340731}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792526146129,"responseId":"gen-1792526146-4N09UtyK0NKzVzY3o7np","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9fdfa74d0e7a4b129b2a7748","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"tests/ablate_cli.rs:23:    let dir = std::env::temp_